import {IZkSyncStateTreeVerifier} from "@hiero-ledger/clpr/verifiers/evm/zksync/lib/IZkSyncStateTreeVerifier.sol";

/// @title ZkSyncStateTreeVerifier
/// @notice Verifies `zks_getProof` storage proofs against a ZKsync Era (EraVM) state-tree root. Deployed
///         once and shared by every ZK Stack verifier; it holds no state.
///
/// ## The tree (zksync-era `core/lib/merkle_tree`, checked at commit ff5f519, 2026-08-25)
/// - Key: `blake2s(address left-padded to 32 bytes ‖ slot)` (`StorageKey::raw_hashed_key`), read as a
///   LITTLE-endian U256 (`hashed_key_u256`). Bit `d` of that integer chooses the side at depth `d`, depth 0
///   being the leaf level (`fold_merkle_path`: bit set → `hash(sibling ‖ node)`).
/// - Leaf: `blake2s(leafIndex as 8 bytes big-endian ‖ value)`; an absent key is the empty leaf
///   `blake2s(0^40)` (index 0, value 0).
/// - Branch: `blake2s(left ‖ right)`. Empty subtree of depth `d + 1`: `blake2s(e_d ‖ e_d)`.
/// - `zks_getProof` returns the siblings root-to-leaf (`metadata_calculator/src/api_server/mod.rs` reverses
///   the tree's leaf-to-root path) and omits the empty-subtree siblings nearest the leaf.
/// - A proof with leaf index 0 must carry value 0 (`TreeEntryWithProof::verify`).
///
/// ## Why no precompile
/// Hedera's BLAKE2F precompile (EIP-152, address 0x09) is the Blake2b F function: 64-bit words, 12
/// rounds, rotations 32/24/16/63 and a different IV. Blake2s uses 32-bit words, 10 rounds and rotations
/// 16/12/8/7, so BLAKE2F cannot compute it. Blake2s runs here in plain EVM code.
///
/// ## How Blake2s is computed
/// Every hash in a proof is a single 64-byte block (branches and key derivation) or a single padded
/// 40-byte block (leaves), so only the final-block compression is needed. The 4×4 state is kept as four
/// row words; word `i` of a row sits in bits `[64i, 64i+32)` of its row, so one G step runs on four columns
/// (then four diagonals) at once. Message word `k` sits zero-padded in its own memory slot at
/// `M_BASE + 32k`, so `mload(M_BASE + 32k + 8i)` yields it already placed in lane `i`. The rounds are
/// generated by `script/zksync/generateBlake2s.ts`.
///
/// Node hashes stay in that lane form between levels; only the root, the key inputs, the leaf and the
/// siblings cross the boundary. Siblings arrive in W-form (see {IZkSyncStateTreeVerifier}) so each one is
/// spread into message slots with shifts only. The empty-subtree hashes are a 256-entry W-form table
/// generated from the definition above.
///
/// ## Records
/// A proof of six or seven entries costs about 2M gas per entry, which together with the L1 half nears
/// Hedera's 15M limit. {recordStorage} proves entries in a separate transaction and stores `keccak256(value)`
/// under `keccak256(root ‖ account ‖ key)`; a later proof marks such an entry with `pathLen = RECORDED`
/// and pays one SLOAD for it. A record is a statement about `root` only, so recording needs no
/// permission: whoever later relies on it still has to authenticate `root`.
///
/// @dev Memory: `verifyStorage` owns memory. It copies the table to 0x80 (and asserts that), keeps the
///      root at 0x20a0 with the record-key scratch after it, the message slots at 0x2100–0x22ff (zero above
///      each word, and 0x2300–0x231f zero), the root and key lanes at 0x2340–0x23bf, and writes the
///      result at 0x2400. The assembly is therefore not marked memory-safe.
